\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 37. Example outreach logic\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 For a challenger brand:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "We noticed your products are already generating meaningful Amazon UK demand..."\
Then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "We operate through an existing Amazon UK Vendor relationship and Mercenta, a self-service wholesale distribution platform..."\
Then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "We're interested in testing a small number of proven ASINs rather than asking you to commit your entire range."\
Then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "Would you be open to discussing who currently owns Amazon UK supply for the brand?"\
That last question is important because it avoids falsely assuming the existing supply relationship.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
